-- Several WITH arguments on one call, in the places a printed module must re-parse
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md, the print defect of section 3.2.1's differential).
-- Every default here is a literal (HAIRCUT, 2026-10-12): the call sites, not the
-- defaults, are what has several arguments.

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
combine MEANS a PLUS b

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
pair MEANS x TIMES y

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

-- several arguments inside brackets, one nested in another, and spliced after other text
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
total MEANS (combine WITH a IS n, b IS 1) PLUS (pair WITH x IS (combine WITH a IS 2, b IS 3), y IS n) PLUS (scaled WITH base IS n, rate IS 2)

#ASSERT (scaled WITH base IS 10, rate IS 2) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (scaled WITH base IS 10) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT (total 4) EQUALS 33
